    "main_topic": [
      {
        "h_title": "An independent travel guide to\nPhitsanulok",
        "main_title": "An independent travel guide to\nPhitsanulok",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 1,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "P’lok will do just fine",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Published/Last edited on 27th July, 2026.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "An ancient centre of Thai culture and politics set along the Nan River, Phitsanulok (or P’Lok for short) today is a busy, dynamic city and one of the larger of Thailand’s provincial capitals. While most travellers see it only through the window of a bus or train enroute to Chiang Mai, those who hop off will find enough to do and eat for a solid break from the tourist trail.",
            "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/location/thailand/northern_thailand/chiang_mai/chiang_mai",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/location/thailand/northern_thailand/chiang_mai/chiang_mai",
                "anchor_text": "Chiang Mai"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Browse hotels in Phitsanulok on Agoda",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Provided by Travelfish partner Agoda.",
            "url": "http://www.agoda.com/partners/tracking.aspx?cid=1742115&url=https://www.agoda.com/city/phitsanulok-th.html&tag=location-291",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "http://www.agoda.com/partners/tracking.aspx?cid=1742115&url=https://www.agoda.com/city/phitsanulok-th.html&tag=location-291",
                "anchor_text": "Agoda"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Often cited as one of Thailand’s oldest (if not the oldest) continuously occupied city, the area was first settled by Khmer people as early as the 10th century. In the mid 1300s, the capital of the Sukhothai Kingdom was moved here, and the Ayutthaya Kingdom temporarily made Phitsanulok its capital around a century later. As late as 1775, the city was a strategic defensive outpost during several military attacks from Burma.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "One of the most revered kings of Thai history, Naresuan, was born in Phitsanulok in 1555. His much-romanticised story of being captured by the Burmese as a boy and later returning to Ayutthaya to defeat his former captors in battle is now the subject of a series of Thai film epics. You can visit his birthplace at Wang Chan Palace and view murals depicting key scenes from his life at Wat Phra Si Rattana Mahathat, which also houses an exquisite 700-year-old Buddha image.",
            "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naresuan",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naresuan",
                "anchor_text": "Naresuan"
              },
              {
                "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/sight_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/phitsanulok/phitsanulok/219",
                "anchor_text": "Wat Phra Si Rattana Mahathat"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Though a handful of other ancient features are scattered around Phitsanulok, today it’s a modern urban centre with bustling streets lined by cement shophouses, some great markets and often not-so-great hotels. Several universities keep the atmosphere lively, especially on Ong Dam Road, and a long riverside promenade offers a breather from ... Travelfish members only please log in below to continue reading. The full text is around 700 words.)",
            "url": "http://www.agoda.com/partners/tracking.aspx?cid=17598&url=https://www.agoda.com/city/phitsanulok-th.html&tag=phitsanulok",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "http://www.agoda.com/partners/tracking.aspx?cid=17598&url=https://www.agoda.com/city/phitsanulok-th.html&tag=phitsanulok",
                "anchor_text": "not-so-great hotels"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
