      {
        "h_title": "Who will Phitsanulok appeal to?",
        "main_title": "An independent travel guide to\nPhitsanulok",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 5,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "While Phitsanulok doesn’t have an oversupply of things to see and do, it does have enough of a bit of everything to keep most visitors happy. If you’re considering a stay in Phitsanulok, then chances are you’re a bit of a slower traveller, and you’re biding your time before pushing on to Sukhothai. In this case, wander the town, enjoy its food, and be sure to spend the evening by the river—there are plenty of good spots to lose an evening to good food and cold drinks.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "How long should you spend in Phitsanulok?",
        "main_title": "An independent travel guide to\nPhitsanulok",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 5,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Many treat Phitsanulok as a transit point, arriving on a morning train, seeing a couple of the central sights and then getting an afternoon onwards bus to Sukhothai. This approach works, but if time is on your side, we feel that Phitsanulok is worth at least an overnight stay thanks to its handful of attractions and genuine urban-Thai atmosphere. If you’re planning on heading to Thung Salaeng Luang or Phu Hin Rong Kla national parks, you’ll need to add at least an extra day for each—longer still if you plan to overnight in either park.",
            "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/sight_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/phitsanulok/phitsanulok/516",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/sight_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/phitsanulok/phitsanulok/516",
                "anchor_text": "Thung Salaeng Luang"
              },
              {
                "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/sight_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/phitsanulok/phitsanulok/515",
                "anchor_text": "Phu Hin Rong Kla"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "What is the best time to go to Phitsanulok?",
        "main_title": "An independent travel guide to\nPhitsanulok",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 5,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Phitsanulok shares the same climate as most of central and northern Thailand, which means November through to late February will give you the best combination of warm though not crazy hot temperatures and little to no rain. By April it will get uncomfortably hot and you’ll get more of the haze from the burning of fields, and by June the rains will start—not ebbing till October. If you want to see the waterfalls at Thung Salaeng Luang at full strength, then September and October are the best time of the year to visit.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "What is the best thing to see or do in Phitsanulok?",
        "main_title": "An independent travel guide to\nPhitsanulok",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 5,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "In downtown Phitsanulok, the two “must sees” are the beautiful Wat Phra Si Rattana Mahathat and the more quirky Sgt. Maj. Thawee Folk Museum. These are both quite conveniently located—the temple is just a short walk from the train station. If you’d like to see one of the national parks, but can’t decide which, we’d say if you’re more a nature fan, then Thung Salaeng Luang is a good choice, but if you like hiking and have an interest in history, then Phu Hin Rong Kla is probably the better bet.",
            "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/sight_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/phitsanulok/phitsanulok/219",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/sight_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/phitsanulok/phitsanulok/219",
                "anchor_text": "Wat Phra Si Rattana Mahathat"
              },
              {
                "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/sight_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/phitsanulok/phitsanulok/220",
                "anchor_text": "Sgt. Maj. Thawee Folk Museum"
              },
              {
                "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/sight_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/phitsanulok/phitsanulok/516",
                "anchor_text": "Thung Salaeng Luang"
              },
              {
                "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/sight_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/phitsanulok/phitsanulok/515",
                "anchor_text": "Phu Hin Rong Kla"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
